<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Monzón</h1><p class="st-meta">943 CE – 1028 CE (approx.) · capital Monzón de Campos</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Leonese frontier county on the Tierra de Campos, created for the Ansúrez family as a counterweight to Castile.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 943 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramiro-ii-of-leon">Ramiro II of León</a> created the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monzon-de-campos">Monzón</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monzon">Monzón</a> de Campos near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a>, for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur-fernandez">Assur Fernández</a>, a rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernan-gonzalez-of-castile">Fernán González of Castile</a>. It was part of the king's effort to check the growing independence of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Ansúrez counts governed a fertile plain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tierra-de-campos">Tierra de Campos</a>, newly resettled by farmers, from the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monzon-de-campos">Monzón</a>. They were among the leading nobles of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-leon">Kingdom of León</a>, involved in its civil wars and frontier fighting against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Caliphate of Córdoba</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After Fernando Ansúrez, the county passed by marriage and conflict into the hands of other families and was absorbed into the domains of the kings of León and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> by the early 11th century. The Ansúrez family later produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ansurez">Pedro Ansúrez</a>, the lord who developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valladolid">Valladolid</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 943 CE – 1028 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:78.47%;width:1.69%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>943 CE – 1028 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Monzón de Campos</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Assur Fernández, Fernando Ansúrez</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Condado de Monzón</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=986&amp;focus=county-of-monzon" aria-label="County of Monzón on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4571 679 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Monzón lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4891 935L4865 919"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4865 919h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4891 935h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4891 935h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Monzón de Campos. <a href="/atlas?year=986&amp;focus=county-of-monzon">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
